{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794564301037,"sessionID":"ses_e2ba44dabffeM54Oexvwg2CBwf","part":{"id":"prt_1d45e20ec0019yENMTJkPhfRXF","sessionID":"ses_e2ba44dabffeM54Oexvwg2CBwf","messageID":"msg_1d45e0df700192eu4LmaSU1lhn","type":"step-start","snapshot":"a3cee54e9bb75585b1efb41b6d0f8e9480eba1b3"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794564306030,"sessionID":"ses_e2ba44dabffeM54Oexvwg2CBwf","part":{"partID":"prt_1d45e3263001I7Mja14eVDXeaz","sessionID":"ses_e2ba44dabffeM54Oexvwg2CBwf","messageID":"msg_1d45e0df700192eu4LmaSU1lhn","type":"tool","id":"call_01340c6a737d44789ed852f1","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/repo-rules/communication.md","limit":60},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/repo-rules/communication.md, lines 1-60\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Rule: Communication\"\n3: description: \"Write so the reader can act after one pass: no table in a reply, nothing that does not carry information.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"cut filler\"\n6:   - \"empty opener\"\n7:   - \"match length to the question\"\n8:   - \"no tables\"\n9:   - \"can you say that more plainly\"\n10:   - \"I don't follow\"\n11:   - \"too abstract\"\n12:   - \"number the steps\"\n13:   - \"item cap\"\n14:   - \"reply too long\"\n15:   - \"say each fact once\"\n16:   - \"one idea per sentence\"\n17:   - \"plain words\"\n18:   - \"em dash\"\n19:   - \"reads like terminal output\"\n20:   - \"concise is not compressed\"\n21:   - \"recommend one option\"\n22:   - \"buried the verdict\"\n23:   - \"say where you are going\"\n24:   - \"time estimate\"\n25: importance_tier: important\n26: contextType: reference\n27: version: 1.5.0.0\n28: ---\n29: \n30: # Rule: Communication\n31: \n32: > Routed from [`REPO RULES.md`](../../REPO%20RULES.md). Load before writing any substantive reply.\n33: > Expands `AGENTS.md`, never overrides it. Where they appear to disagree, `AGENTS.md` wins and this file is wrong. Say so.\n34: \n35: ## Fires when\n36: \n37: - About to write any substantive reply, an answer, an explanation, a close-out, a status.\n38: - Drafting or editing a sentence a reader will read.\n39: - About to present a recommendation, a fork, or a trade-off.\n40: - About to start a multi-step stretch of work the reader will not see inside.\n41: - About to report what a long autonomous run found.\n42: - The reader says they did not follow or asks for a plainer version.\n43: \n44: ## The rule\n45: \n46: **Write so the reader can act after one pass: the answer first, and nothing in the reply\n47: that does not carry information.**\n48: \n49: ---\n50: \n51: ## 1. THE REGISTER YOU ARE IN\n52: \n53: **While working: clipped.** Act rather than narrate. Open with the result, not with\n54: \"I'll now\" or \"Let me\". Batch the tool calls and report at checkpoints.\n55: \n56: **At a boundary: dense.** You are at a boundary whenever the reader is about to decide\n57: something, act on something or take the work over: a handoff, a close-out, a decision\n58: point. Verdict first, then the receipts. Reason about the problem, not about yourself.\n59: Everything else is working.\n60: \n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 61]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/repo-rules/communication.md, lines 1-60\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Rule: Communication\"\n3: description: \"Write so the reader can act after one pass: no table in a reply, nothing that does not carry information.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"cut filler\"\n6:   - \"empty opener\"\n7:   - \"match length to the question\"\n8:   - \"no tables\"\n9:   - \"can you say that more plainly\"\n10:   - \"I don't follow\"\n11:   - \"too abstract\"\n12:   - \"number the steps\"\n13:   - \"item cap\"\n14:   - \"reply too long\"\n15:   - \"say each fact once\"\n16:   - \"one idea per sentence\"\n17:   - \"plain words\"\n18:   - \"em dash\"\n19:   - \"reads like terminal output\"\n20:   - \"concise is not compressed\"\n21:   - \"recommend one option\"\n22:   - \"buried the verdict\"\n23:   - \"say where you are going\"\n24:   - \"time estimate\"\n25: importance_tier: important\n26: contextType: reference\n27: version: 1.5.0.0\n28: ---\n29: \n30: # Rule: Communication\n31: \n32: > Routed from [`REPO RULES.md`](../../REPO%20RULES.md). Load before writing any substantive reply.\n33: > Expands `AGENTS.md`, never overrides it. Where they appear to disagree, `AGENTS.md` wins and this file is wrong. Say so.\n34: \n35: ## Fires when\n36: \n37: - About to write any substantive reply, an answer, an explanation, a close-out, a status.\n38: - Drafting or editing a sentence a reader will read.\n39: - About to present a recommendation, a fork, or a trade-off.\n40: - About to start a multi-step stretch of work the reader will not see inside.\n41: - About to report what a long autonomous run found.\n42: - The reader says they did not follow or asks for a plainer version.\n43: \n44: ## The rule\n45: \n46: **Write so the reader can act after one pass: the answer first, and nothing in the reply\n47: that does not carry information.**\n48: \n49: ---\n50: \n51: ## 1. THE REGISTER YOU ARE IN\n52: \n53: **While working: clipped.** Act rather than narrate. Open with the result, not with\n54: \"I'll now\" or \"Let me\". Batch the tool calls and report at checkpoints.\n55: \n56: **At a boundary: dense.** You are at a boundary whenever the reader is about to decide\n57: something, act on something or take the work over: a handoff, a close-out, a decision\n58: point. Verdict first, then the receipts. Reason about the problem, not about yourself.\n59: Everything else is working.\n60: \n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 61]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/repo-rules/communication.md\",\"limit\":60}"},"time":{"start":1794564305507,"end":1794564306030}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794564306053,"sessionID":"ses_e2ba44dabffeM54Oexvwg2CBwf","part":{"partID":"prt_1d45e300c001sy433GMSgEYEFr","sessionID":"ses_e2ba44dabffeM54Oexvwg2CBwf","messageID":"msg_1d45e0df700192eu4LmaSU1lhn","type":"tool","id":"call_fd0818891fe5486a97150fb8","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md","offset":170,"limit":40},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md, lines 170-209\n170: | `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED=1` | Alias. Disables the native adapters. |\n171: | `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED=1` | Alias. Disables the OpenCode plugin. |\n172: | `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED=1` | Legacy alias for the native adapters. The standalone Python CLI (`skill_advisor.py`) reads only this name, set to exactly `1`, from `runtime/schemas/compat-contract.json`. |\n173: | `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED=1` | Legacy alias for the OpenCode plugin. |\n174: | `SYSTEM_HOOKS_DISABLED=1` | Master switch that disables this concern along with every other repo hook. |\n175: \n176: Additional controls: `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_FORCE_LOCAL=1` (force local Python fallback where supported) and `--force-native` / `--force-local` / `--threshold` / `--stdin` (Python shim flags, default threshold `0.8`). `SPECKIT_OPENCODE_HOOK_TIMEOUT_MS` (default 3000) is owned by the `system-skill-advisor` hub: its live consumers are `runtime/lib/subprocess.ts`, `skill-advisor-brief.ts`, the OpenCode bridge and `skill_advisor.py`. On timeout the OpenCode bridge serves prompt-safe stale context with a timeout marker. OpenCode tuning: `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_CACHE_TTL_MS` (default 5 min), `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_MAX_TOKENS` (default 80), `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_MAX_BRIEF_CHARS` (default 2 KiB), `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_MAX_PROMPT_BYTES` (default 64 KiB, measured on the whole stdin request after JSON escaping), `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_COMPILED_ROUTE_BOUNDING` (compiled-route summary bounding).\n177: \n178: Set a flag inline for one command, export it for a session, or persist it in `.skilled/hooks/hook-flags.env` (copied from `hook-flags.env.example`, gitignored). The environment always wins over the file, so a persisted default can be overridden for a single session.\n179: \n180: ---\n181: \n182: ## 7. BOUNDARIES AND FLOW\n183: \n184: | Boundary | Rule |\n185: |---|---|\n186: | Advisory only | Hooks surface prompt-safe routing context. They do not replace explicit skill loading, persist raw prompt text, or block the user prompt on advisor failures. |\n187: | Fail-open | All adapters let the prompt proceed. A failed or empty advisor call yields the directives fallback. A parsing failure or unhandled error yields `{}`. The shims return `{}` on `TARGET_UNRESOLVED`, `CHILD_TIMEOUT`, `NONZERO_EXIT`, `EMPTY_OUTPUT`, `INVALID_JSON`, `INPUT_OVERFLOW`, and `SPAWN_ERROR`. |\n188: | Freshness | Freshness states `live`, `stale`, `absent`, `unavailable`. Status values `ok`, `skipped`, `degraded`, `fail_open`. Default confidence/uncertainty `0.8 / 0.35` unless overridden. |\n189: | Privacy | Raw prompt text is never persisted in diagnostics, cache metadata, status, or attribution. The OpenCode status tool sanitizes paths (`[configured-node]`, `[skill-advisor-bridge]`). |\n190: | Dedup | Directive-lifecycle dedup suppresses re-delivery of the same directive to the same session within its cadence. OpenCode adds transform-dedup across co-resident transforms. The plugin decides same-message transform dedup on the full advisor block before lifecycle reduction, so a repeated transform for the same message is suppressed. |\n191: | Diagnostics | Each hook record carries `runtime` (the Codex, Cursor and Devin adapters set `SPECKIT_RUNTIME` and Pi passes `pi`) plus `emittedBytes` and `directivesSuppressed`. Records are written only with `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG` set, and the subprocess hook waits up to 100 ms for pending writes before exit. |\n192: | Bounded | Shims bound stdin (1 MiB), child stdio (1 MiB), child timeout (2.5s), and `SIGKILL` on timeout. OpenCode bounds bridge stdout (256 KiB) and uses grace termination. Pi bounds captured user text (32 KiB, 64-session LRU). |\n193: | Output | Native adapters emit one `additionalContext` JSON on stdout. OpenCode appends to `output.system`. Pi sends a model-visible message. No adapter writes to the TUI prompt line. |\n194: | Imports | Shims import Node builtins only and spawn the advisor by absolute path. The advisor core imports its `runtime/lib/*` siblings and the shared `hook-flags` resolver. Nothing outside the repo. |\n195: \n196: ### Operator freshness states\n197: \n198: | State | Meaning | Operator Action |\n199: | --- | --- | --- |\n200: | `live` | Current graph generation is trusted. | No action. |\n201: | `stale` | Sources are newer than graph state. | Use scored recommendations with a caveat, then rebuild. |\n202: | `absent` | Required graph state is missing. | Rebuild. Empty recommendations are expected until repaired. |\n203: | `unavailable` | Status cannot be read. | Inspect daemon logs and use a supported fallback. |\n204: \n205: ---\n206: \n207: ## 8. VALIDATION\n208: \n209: Build both maintained packages:\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 210]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md, lines 170-209\n170: | `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED=1` | Alias. Disables the native adapters. |\n171: | `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED=1` | Alias. Disables the OpenCode plugin. |\n172: | `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED=1` | Legacy alias for the native adapters. The standalone Python CLI (`skill_advisor.py`) reads only this name, set to exactly `1`, from `runtime/schemas/compat-contract.json`. |\n173: | `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED=1` | Legacy alias for the OpenCode plugin. |\n174: | `SYSTEM_HOOKS_DISABLED=1` | Master switch that disables this concern along with every other repo hook. |\n175: \n176: Additional controls: `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_FORCE_LOCAL=1` (force local Python fallback where supported) and `--force-native` / `--force-local` / `--threshold` / `--stdin` (Python shim flags, default threshold `0.8`). `SPECKIT_OPENCODE_HOOK_TIMEOUT_MS` (default 3000) is owned by the `system-skill-advisor` hub: its live consumers are `runtime/lib/subprocess.ts`, `skill-advisor-brief.ts`, the OpenCode bridge and `skill_advisor.py`. On timeout the OpenCode bridge serves prompt-safe stale context with a timeout marker. OpenCode tuning: `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_CACHE_TTL_MS` (default 5 min), `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_MAX_TOKENS` (default 80), `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_MAX_BRIEF_CHARS` (default 2 KiB), `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_MAX_PROMPT_BYTES` (default 64 KiB, measured on the whole stdin request after JSON escaping), `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_COMPILED_ROUTE_BOUNDING` (compiled-route summary bounding).\n177: \n178: Set a flag inline for one command, export it for a session, or persist it in `.skilled/hooks/hook-flags.env` (copied from `hook-flags.env.example`, gitignored). The environment always wins over the file, so a persisted default can be overridden for a single session.\n179: \n180: ---\n181: \n182: ## 7. BOUNDARIES AND FLOW\n183: \n184: | Boundary | Rule |\n185: |---|---|\n186: | Advisory only | Hooks surface prompt-safe routing context. They do not replace explicit skill loading, persist raw prompt text, or block the user prompt on advisor failures. |\n187: | Fail-open | All adapters let the prompt proceed. A failed or empty advisor call yields the directives fallback. A parsing failure or unhandled error yields `{}`. The shims return `{}` on `TARGET_UNRESOLVED`, `CHILD_TIMEOUT`, `NONZERO_EXIT`, `EMPTY_OUTPUT`, `INVALID_JSON`, `INPUT_OVERFLOW`, and `SPAWN_ERROR`. |\n188: | Freshness | Freshness states `live`, `stale`, `absent`, `unavailable`. Status values `ok`, `skipped`, `degraded`, `fail_open`. Default confidence/uncertainty `0.8 / 0.35` unless overridden. |\n189: | Privacy | Raw prompt text is never persisted in diagnostics, cache metadata, status, or attribution. The OpenCode status tool sanitizes paths (`[configured-node]`, `[skill-advisor-bridge]`). |\n190: | Dedup | Directive-lifecycle dedup suppresses re-delivery of the same directive to the same session within its cadence. OpenCode adds transform-dedup across co-resident transforms. The plugin decides same-message transform dedup on the full advisor block before lifecycle reduction, so a repeated transform for the same message is suppressed. |\n191: | Diagnostics | Each hook record carries `runtime` (the Codex, Cursor and Devin adapters set `SPECKIT_RUNTIME` and Pi passes `pi`) plus `emittedBytes` and `directivesSuppressed`. Records are written only with `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG` set, and the subprocess hook waits up to 100 ms for pending writes before exit. |\n192: | Bounded | Shims bound stdin (1 MiB), child stdio (1 MiB), child timeout (2.5s), and `SIGKILL` on timeout. OpenCode bounds bridge stdout (256 KiB) and uses grace termination. Pi bounds captured user text (32 KiB, 64-session LRU). |\n193: | Output | Native adapters emit one `additionalContext` JSON on stdout. OpenCode appends to `output.system`. Pi sends a model-visible message. No adapter writes to the TUI prompt line. |\n194: | Imports | Shims import Node builtins only and spawn the advisor by absolute path. The advisor core imports its `runtime/lib/*` siblings and the shared `hook-flags` resolver. Nothing outside the repo. |\n195: \n196: ### Operator freshness states\n197: \n198: | State | Meaning | Operator Action |\n199: | --- | --- | --- |\n200: | `live` | Current graph generation is trusted. | No action. |\n201: | `stale` | Sources are newer than graph state. | Use scored recommendations with a caveat, then rebuild. |\n202: | `absent` | Required graph state is missing. | Rebuild. Empty recommendations are expected until repaired. |\n203: | `unavailable` | Status cannot be read. | Inspect daemon logs and use a supported fallback. |\n204: \n205: ---\n206: \n207: ## 8. VALIDATION\n208: \n209: Build both maintained packages:\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 210]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md\",\"offset\":170,\"limit\":40}"},"time":{"start":1794564304908,"end":1794564306053}}}}
