{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794564316945,"sessionID":"ses_e2ba44dabffeM54Oexvwg2CBwf","part":{"partID":"prt_1d45e59af00166ttmA10E4dUfq","sessionID":"ses_e2ba44dabffeM54Oexvwg2CBwf","messageID":"msg_1d45e40db0011RIVO1GA0CVmrC","type":"tool","id":"call_fa189183b3e34d819f39468f","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md","oldString":"Records are written only with `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG` set, and the subprocess hook waits up to 100 ms for pending writes before exit.","newString":"Every prompt writes a health record to the diagnostics sink with no prompt, skill label or error text, and an answer from the CLI's local scorer carries `degraded: true`. `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG` adds the skill label and the error text. The subprocess hook waits up to 100 ms for pending writes before exit."},"output":"Edited .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md","patch":"Index: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md\n===================================================================\n--- .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md\n+++ .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md\n@@ -187,9 +187,9 @@\n | Fail-open | All adapters let the prompt proceed. A failed or empty advisor call yields the directives fallback. A parsing failure or unhandled error yields `{}`. The shims return `{}` on `TARGET_UNRESOLVED`, `CHILD_TIMEOUT`, `NONZERO_EXIT`, `EMPTY_OUTPUT`, `INVALID_JSON`, `INPUT_OVERFLOW`, and `SPAWN_ERROR`. |\n | Freshness | Freshness states `live`, `stale`, `absent`, `unavailable`. Status values `ok`, `skipped`, `degraded`, `fail_open`. Default confidence/uncertainty `0.8 / 0.35` unless overridden. |\n | Privacy | Raw prompt text is never persisted in diagnostics, cache metadata, status, or attribution. The OpenCode status tool sanitizes paths (`[configured-node]`, `[skill-advisor-bridge]`). |\n | Dedup | Directive-lifecycle dedup suppresses re-delivery of the same directive to the same session within its cadence. OpenCode adds transform-dedup across co-resident transforms. The plugin decides same-message transform dedup on the full advisor block before lifecycle reduction, so a repeated transform for the same message is suppressed. |\n-| Diagnostics | Each hook record carries `runtime` (the Codex, Cursor and Devin adapters set `SPECKIT_RUNTIME` and Pi passes `pi`) plus `emittedBytes` and `directivesSuppressed`. Records are written only with `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG` set, and the subprocess hook waits up to 100 ms for pending writes before exit. |\n+| Diagnostics | Each hook record carries `runtime` (the Codex, Cursor and Devin adapters set `SPECKIT_RUNTIME` and Pi passes `pi`) plus `emittedBytes` and `directivesSuppressed`. Every prompt writes a health record to the diagnostics sink with no prompt, skill label or error text, and an answer from the CLI's local scorer carries `degraded: true`. `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG` adds the skill label and the error text. The subprocess hook waits up to 100 ms for pending writes before exit. |\n | Bounded | Shims bound stdin (1 MiB), child stdio (1 MiB), child timeout (2.5s), and `SIGKILL` on timeout. OpenCode bounds bridge stdout (256 KiB) and uses grace termination. Pi bounds captured user text (32 KiB, 64-session LRU). |\n | Output | Native adapters emit one `additionalContext` JSON on stdout. OpenCode appends to `output.system`. Pi sends a model-visible message. No adapter writes to the TUI prompt line. |\n | Imports | Shims import Node builtins only and spawn the advisor by absolute path. The advisor core imports its `runtime/lib/*` siblings and the shared `hook-flags` resolver. Nothing outside the repo. |\n \n","status":"modified","additions":1,"deletions":1}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md\",\"oldString\":\"Records are written only with `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG` set, and the subprocess hook waits up to 100 ms for pending writes before exit.\",\"newString\":\"Every prompt writes a health record to the diagnostics sink with no prompt, skill label or error text, and an answer from the CLI's local scorer carries `degraded: true`. `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG` adds the skill label and the error text. The subprocess hook waits up to 100 ms for pending writes before exit.\"}"},"time":{"start":1794564315567,"end":1794564316945}}}}
