{"type":"text","timestamp":1794564349919,"sessionID":"ses_e2ba44dabffeM54Oexvwg2CBwf","part":{"id":"prt_1d45ede86001AB1fd3DI5sciUz","sessionID":"ses_e2ba44dabffeM54Oexvwg2CBwf","messageID":"msg_1d45ec52e001riv2aBM2BsW113","type":"text","text":"T008 is done.\n\n**File written:** `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md` — replaced the Diagnostics-row sentence that began \"Records are written only with\" with the required default-record text, keeping `degraded: true` and `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG` in backticks.\n\n**Verify output:**\n\n```\n--- rg written only with:\nexit=1            (no match, prints nothing)\n--- rg adds the skill label:\n1\nexit=0\n```\n\nBoth conditions hold: `rg -c \"written only with\"` printed nothing, and `rg -c \"adds the skill label and the error text\"` printed exactly 1.\n\n**Notes:**\n- `git status` on the file shows only `M` for the one named file; no other file was touched.\n- `git` was used read-only (`status` only). Nothing was committed, staged, or reverted.\n- The checkbox in `tasks.md` was not ticked, per instructions.\n- Routing record: the trigger index returned no hits; the skill advisor routed to `sk-doc` at 0.906 confidence, and the sk-doc compiled route returned `defer` with no targets (the hub has no default mode). Since the task line supplies the exact replacement text and the dispatched worker cannot ask, the edit was made directly under the file's existing table style.\n- One deviation for the orchestrator to consider: the sk-doc router has no mode packet for a targeted sentence edit of an existing reference doc, so it defers. If that is unintended, the fix belongs in `sk-doc/mode-registry.json` (a prose-edit mode or alias), not in this phase's task list.","time":{"start":1794564349574,"end":1794564349919}}}
